s, by defining exactly when the mandates kick in.\n    *   Is it efficient? Extremely. It prevents \"regulatory bloat\" during the exploratory phase.\n    *   Is it feasible? Yes, a sign-off gate is a standard industry practice (CI/CD pipelines).\n    *   Does it protect scientific ambition? Yes, researchers aren't bogged down by rigid logging requirements for every failed hypothesis.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal optimizes resource allocation by preventing the costly application of industrial-grade logging to transient exploratory research while creating a clear, low-overhead mechanism to ensure compliance before deployment. It balances regulatory risk with scientific agility.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (very high because it directly addresses the core tension between R&D speed and regulatory burden).",
