ategic value (scientific influence/leadership).\n        *   Operational efficiency (standardized documentation reduces redundant effort across different teams).\n        *   Directly addresses the \"technical documentation\" requirement of Recital 71 and Article 12.\n\n    *   *Negative:*\n        *   \"Going well beyond the Act's minimums\" could be seen as scope creep or wasteful expenditure if the goal is *only* compliance.\n        *   Maintaining an open-source project requires ongoing resources (community portal).\n\n    *   As Lab Director, I want efficiency and influence. This proposal turns a regulatory burden (documentation) into a strategic asset (a standard). It's a \"force multiplier.\" Instead of every team inventing their own way to record hyperparameters or data lineage for the EU AI Act, they use one machine-readable schema.\n\n    *   Rationale: Standardizing documentation through a machine-readable schema transforms a regulatory burden into an operational efficiency and a strategic asset for scientific leadership. The limited initial time investment is justified by the potential for reduced redundancy across all high-risk projects.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 85 (Strong, but not 100 because of the long-term maintenance commitment of an open community portal).",
