ing compliance spending.\n    *   Are there risks? Some might argue a flat percentage is arbitrary, but as a Compliance Officer, having *some* guaranteed budget is far better than none.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal addresses the critical risk of underfunding mandatory technical requirements (logging/record-keeping) by institutionalizing them as upfront budgetary constraints, ensuring regulatory compliance doesn't become an afterthought that threatens project viability or institutional legality.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High. It transforms a legal requirement into an operational reality.",
