entific impact\" (via real-world application) is zero. Therefore, early feasibility is aligned with ensuring the research actually reaches the world.\n\n    *Wait*, let's reconsider the \"external compliance consultant\" part. Having an external non-scientist score a go/no-go for funding can be anathema to scientific autonomy. But it's limited to Annex III (High Risk) products, not general basic research.\n\n    Rationale: This prevents the waste of critical compute and personnel resources on architectures that are fundamentally incompatible with legal requirements, ensuring lab capacity is dedicated to impactful, deployable research. The administrative overhead is minimal compared to the risk of pursuing a scientific dead-end due to regulatory non-compliance.\n    Decision: approve.\n    Promise: 70.",
