hout the lifetime of the AI system.\"\n    *   Article 12 focuses more on *automatic logs*, but Recital 71 provides the context for the broader record-keeping requirement that Article 12 supports.\n    *   P2798 addresses the documentation part of Recital 71 directly.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* While assigning a dedicated steward per system is resource-heavy, this framework establishes a necessary compliance baseline to avoid catastrophic regulatory failure and leverages standard version-control infrastructure. It transforms an abstract legal requirement into a manageable operational process.\n    *   *Decision:* Approve. (It's essentially mandatory for high-risk systems; you can't just ignore Recital 71).\n    *   *Promise:* High, because it is low-risk and necessary, though the human cost of \"stewards\" needs monitoring. Let's say 85.\n\n    *   Check: Did I write rationale *before* decision? Yes.\n    *   Check: Is the id echoed exactly (P2798)? Yes.\n    *   Check: Decision \"approve\"/\"reject\"? Yes.\n    *   Check: Promise integer 0-100? Yes.",
