s in AI safety is hindered.\n        *   *Iteration Speed:* The proposal explicitly mentions keeping \"iteration speed intact\" by decoupling prototype development from long-term storage requirements. This is crucial for R&D researchers who cannot be bogged down by production-grade archival constraints during the ideation/experimentation phase.\n\n    *   The proposal solves a major friction point: the clash between the slow, stable nature of regulatory record-keeping (\"lifetime\") and the fast, unstable nature of AI research (weekly sprints).\n    *   By implementing this as a separate infrastructure layer, researchers can focus on the \"knowledge frontier\" without compromising the legal viability of their work.\n    *   The technical approach (cryptographic content addressing) ensures data integrity, which is essential for any scientific claim regarding system performance over time.\n\n    *   Rationale: This infrastructure decouples rigorous regulatory record-keeping from the rapid iteration cycles of AI research, ensuring that intellectual progress isn't throttled by deployment constraints while providing the high-fidelity traceability necessary for forensic safety analysis.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: High (85-90). It's a sound engineering solution to a regulatory constraint that protects R&D velocity.",
