ile compliance data or redesign their experimental cores every time they changed a parameter (which would happen if logging were baked into the core rather than decoupled), the pace of research would slow down significantly.\n    *   Furthermore, having \"immutable event records\" and precise tracking of reference databases provides high-quality data for ablation studies and reproducibility—core tenets of intellectual merit and scientific impact.\n\n    *   Rationale: The proposal allows for strict regulatory compliance without disrupting the core architectural agility needed for rapid research iteration and prototyping. It also enhances reproducibility by providing immutable, detailed logs of experimental runs in biometric matching.\n    *   Decision: Approve. (It supports the research mission by removing administrative friction and improving data provenance).\n    *   Promise: High. It's a pragmatic engineering fix that preserves scientific velocity.\n\n    *   1-2 sentence rationale.\n    *   \"approve\" or \"reject\".\n    *   Integer 0-100.",
