ilding.\n\n    *   The proposal converts a legal requirement into an engineering primitive. This minimizes the risk of non-compliance during the transition from research to production.\n    *   It specifically targets the high-risk categories (Annex III 1(a)) mentioned in Article 12(3).\n    *   By making it \"native\" to the prototype, it avoids the \"technical debt\" and \"retrofitting\" risks that often lead to compliance failures or delayed launches.\n\n    *   Rationale: This proposal systematically mitigates the risk of non-compliance by automating the implementation of mandatory logging requirements at the point of inception, ensuring Article 12 requirements are not overlooked during rapid iteration.\n    *   Decision: Approve.\n    *   Promise: Very high. It's a pragmatic engineering solution to a legal requirement that removes human error and prevents costly retrofitting. (Score: 95).",
